error[E0323]: `---` is not a value
 --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:6:7
  |
6 |   x = ---
  |       ^^^ only allowed as the initial value of a declaration
help: declare the variable with its type and opt out of zeroing: `buf: [256]U8 = ---`
  = see `wid explain E0323`

error[E0323]: `[4]F32` is a type, not a value
 --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:7:7
  |
7 |   t = [4]F32
  |       ^^^^^^ a type cannot be used as a value here
help: make a zero value with `{}` where `[4]F32` is expected, like `x: [4]F32 = {}`, or write an array literal
  = see `wid explain E0323`

error[E0302]: Wid has no argument spreading
 --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:9:12
  |
9 |   p total(*nums)
  |            ^^^^ `*` cannot spread a collection into arguments
  = note: every method takes a fixed number of arguments
help: pass `nums` as one argument to a parameter of type `[]T`, or pass the elements one by one
  = see `wid explain E0302`

error[E0301]: a range loop binds one variable
  --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:10:7
   |
10 |   for i, j in 0...3
   |       ^^^^ the number is the only value a range gives
help: write `for i in a...b`; `for x, i in xs` gives indexes for arrays and slices
   = see `wid explain E0301`

error[E0321]: a range has no elements to bind by reference
  --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:13:8
   |
13 |   for &k in 0...3
   |        ^ each number is a fresh value
help: bind the number by value
   |   for k in 0...3
   = see `wid explain E0321`

error[E0107]: cannot assign to this expression
  --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:16:3
   |
16 |   total(nums) = 3
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a method call
   |               - assignment here
   = note: a call returns a temporary value, so there is nothing to store into
   = see `wid explain E0107`

error[E0105]: `until` cannot bind a value
  --> tests/ui/value_errors.wid:18:9
   |
18 |   until line = next_line
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this binding would only exist when the value is nil
help: loop with `while v = maybe … end` instead
   = see `wid explain E0105`

